If you haven’t played tablet 2, don’t worry—there’s only one thing you need to
know from it. Words written in ALL CAPITALS are “logograms”, special cuneiform
signs used as shorthand for entire words. The CAPITALS indicate that we’re
transcribing the names of the signs, not the actual Hittite pronunciation.

Good luck!

> 1
1   Nu karimni natta pāun. Nu TUG natta waššiyanun.

What exactly happened to the baker’s garment from the previous tablet is not
clear. The word TUG here might mean “appropriate clothing”—that is, a
disguise—or it could mean that the protagonist discarded his unclean clothing
and is now naked in the inner sanctum.

