> 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 ohhun
Nu DUB 1^KAM ōḫḫun.

Nu F^Gulzawiyaš šiuniyanza kiššan tēt: mān=wa ina UD.20^KAM D^Armaš aki,
nu=wa=kan 2 kupiyatallieš ḫaššun kunanzi. Nu ḫaššuš 5 antuḫšuš kupiyatiya
punušta. Nu parkueššanteš ašantan memiyan memiškanzi.

Hittite had no specific word for “read”: only “look at” and “speak out loud”.
In this case, the narrator seems to be reading silently: he looks at the
tablet, then provides the text of that tablet in the next paragraph.

